  "confirmedCodeDefects": [
    "baseline music error/deadline escalates to owner unavailable and releases healthy environment/effects",
    "incoming play request was treated as playback and could fade out healthy music while incoming was buffering",
    "currentStatus polling can mask the event-only native item error",
    "Screen recovery called before setActive can reject explicit resume; parent Screen regression demonstrates ordering"
  ],
  "conditionalHypothesis": "An old keepAudioSessionActive:false player can schedule global deactivation in a 100ms no-playing window while its replacement buffers. The installed native guard prevents this if any sibling is already playing. Fixture supports the conditional mechanism, not attribution of the reported iPhone silence.",
  "fixes": {
    "session": "shared serialized lease coordinator; all managed native players keepAudioSessionActive:true; last active lease false, new readiness waits repair true",
    "isolation": "music failure retires only its voice; healthy ambience/effects remain; explicit partial music recovery preserves those player identities",
    "recovery": "foreground/user intent only; concurrent recovery coalesces; max2 actual repairs per owner; healthy calls do not spend budget; no frame-driven route restart",
    "clock": "wall-clock load deadline for active lifetime; background/disabled owner retires voice; finite completion uses native currentTime/status where available",
    "resources": {
      "effectPool": 10,
      "maximumMusicPlayers": 2,
      "maximumPerActiveOwner": 12,
      "ownerTimersAdded": 0,
      "diagnosticEventLimit": 64,
      "diagnosticValueTextLimit": 160
    },
    "preferences": "existing silent-switch respecting mode, recording/background off, gain normalization, music/environment/effect/illusion preferences unchanged"
  },
  "limits": [
    "No AVFoundation, real output device, acoustic listening, iPhone route interruption or actual decoder exercised.",
    "Shared-native harness matches audited session semantics but simplifies asset buffering and most finite effect durations to one second; music durations and Shepard12s are modeled.",
    "Synchronous seeks are enabled only for the long App route; controlled deferred seek tests cover asynchronous completion separately.",
    "Generic effect/environment allocation/play/seek exceptions conservatively stop the owner pool and retain exact failure phase; they are not classified as proven native-wide failures or isolated per effect asset.",
    "Missing optional native module records availability:missing-native without inventing an exception; actual probe/import exceptions are retained with ownerId0 because no owner exists yet.",
    "Initial red and intermediate logs retain their historical assertion outcomes. Source hashes below are packaging-time inventory after frozen audio focused runs; final all-project guard and exports belong to parent final verification.",
